# wfg-log 1
# fixture take - a take on a sampling channel: recorded and looped by transport cues,
# its points ridden, a layer laid and undone, held by Esc, looped again by a later mic
# cue, cleared, and a double Esc (namespace draft 19.3 and 19.6, 2026-09-27).
#
# WHAT IT IS FOR: that a take's life replays from the document and the log alone, with
# no interface and no recorder. The standby arm claims Looper for the mic cue "Loop
# voice", whose GO leaves the take waiting (onGo wait). The transport cues Rec and Loop
# it press the take through their GOs - no record of their own - and the recorder's
# close comes back three ticks later as take.closed, in seconds, which is the audio
# side's word, re-injected. The loop points are the channel's session rows, set through
# the tree's door; the layer and its undo are take.overdub, take.loop and take.undo.
# Esc lets go of the channel and the take is held; GO on "Scene 5 loop" (onGo loop)
# takes the channel and loops the take it found; take.clear empties it and a double Esc
# ends the run. Recorded from a real `wfg serve --hosted --input-wav` of a copy of
# tests/fixtures/bundles/take fed a steady level at its first input, driven over OSC by
# tests/blackbox/phase9c_take.py --keep-log.
# bundle take sha256:4804455ab4d41acd12321e31733699ce7f89eb5c2269225807171501b172af4e
